WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.908
After installing Ninai, open Setup guide. The recording uses the real
local interface and sample data.

2
00:00:06.908 --> 00:00:13.908
Add a project decision and create a named project for this work.

3
00:00:13.908 --> 00:00:20.908
Write a short decision and save it under your project. Choose Codex as
the assistant to test.

4
00:00:20.908 --> 00:00:27.864
Choose access, open the assistant card, and enable Read for Launch
rehearsal. Save and Delete stay off.

5
00:00:27.864 --> 00:00:35.114
Turn on Read for Codex. Other project actions remain off.

6
00:00:35.114 --> 00:00:42.114
Send this project-specific request to Codex. A real Codex recall ran
between these recorded scenes.

7
00:00:42.114 --> 00:00:48.114
Open permissions and turn off Read for the same project. Then ask the
assistant to recall again.

8
00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:54.141
Choose project access and disable Read for Codex. Other assistants
keep their own permissions.

9
00:00:54.141 --> 00:01:00.367
Turn off the Read checkbox. Ask Codex to repeat the same request
before checking progress.

10
00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:08.145
Repeat the request after revocation, then check progress. This real
Codex request returned no project memories.

11
00:01:08.145 --> 00:01:14.602
Sharing history shows the successful recall and the denied request,
including purpose and token count.
